<http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/il/NXS24-Figure2.29> a ipbes:Illustration ;
    ipbes:hasDescription "Panel (A) displays beneficial hotspots; panel (B) displays degradation hotspots. Analyses were conducted separately for the marine (top map) and terrestrial (bottom map) realms show in each panel. See data management report for detailed information on data and methods. Beneficial hotspots are areas with high species richness, food production, life expectancy and groundwater volume, whereas degradation hotspots are areas with high threatened species richness, ecological impacts of climate change (climate velocity), malnutrition, DALYs and blue water scarcity." ;
