<http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/il/NXS24-Figure5.3.13> a ipbes:Illustration ;
    ipbes:hasDescription "The practices use technologies to sow crops in large-scale agriculture without using herbicides or tillage practices. Left photo: a machine designed to apply pesticides was modified to create equipment that applies seeds and fertilizers over a mature or green growing crop (e.g., corn). Middle photo: this machine cuts the roots of unwanted plant species 3-12 cm under the soil surface leaving most of the ground cover intact. Right photo: rolling crimper acting on winter service crops (e.g., rye, oat, vetch) generates mechanical drying of the plants and helps prepare the soil and organic cover for summer crops (e.g., corn, soybean). These management practices might be combined with herbicides or tillage in certain moments or years but, in that case, with required frequencies well below the historical use." ;
    dcterms:identifier "Figure5.3.13" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Three examples of conventional practices adapted to meet agroecological needs in Argentina." .

