<http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/il/NXS24-Figure5.3.21> a ipbes:Illustration ;
    ipbes:hasDescription "Interaction scores were characterized by the colour of the intersection box between response options in columns with response options in rows. When the colour of the intersection box is white, this means the interaction score is equal to zero, hence the two response options considered do not exhibit any dependency. On the contrary, when the intersection box colour is dark blue, this means that the interaction score is 3 indicating the highest level of interdependency among the two response options considered. The blue colour box (interaction score = 2) and the light blue colour box (interaction score = 1) respectively represent medium and low levels of dependency between response options." ;
    dcterms:identifier "Figure5.3.21" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Interdependencies between the response options." .

