<http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/il/NXS24-Figure5.4.18> a ipbes:Illustration ;
    ipbes:hasDescription "Response options may be more relevant to a context depending on burden of disease, location and economic development of a country. However, enabling the right to health services (A) and addressing specific disease risks or enablers of a clean, healthy and sustainable environment (B) are both required (note that in B, other options may also be required). Response options may be bundled to address one or more communicable (C) or non-communicable diseases (D), in association with healthcare services (A). One Health and other integrated approaches to education, training and governance and/or Indigenous Peoples’ and local communities’ values can enhance the acceptability and capacity to address nexus challenges (E). Importantly, while the figure focuses on the health-related response options featured in this subchapter, synergies with similar response options from other sectors will strengthen the nexus, e.g., in panel D, F11/C15, Sustainable healthy diets (Chapter 5.3, section 5.3.3.11; Chapter 5.5, section 5.5.3.15) and in panel E, B10, Rights-based approaches (Chapter 5.1, section 5.1.3.10). See also Chapter 5.6 (section 5.6.4, Figure 5.6.5 and Table 5.6.3)." ;
    dcterms:identifier "Figure5.4.18" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Illustrative examples of bundling and sequencing the health response options presented." .

<http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/il/NXS24-Figure5.4.19> a ipbes:Illustration ;
