    ipbes:hasConfidenceLevel "established but incomplete",
        "well established" ;
    ipbes:hasDescription "Negative impacts of food systems on the nexus elements from both land conversion and unsustainable agricultural practices have decreased biodiversity and consequently many of nature’s contributions to people, particularly through diminished regulating contributions (e.g., regulation of water quality and climate) (well established) {2.4.2, 2.5} and increased non-communicable disease risks (well established) {2.4.3, 2.5}, emerging infectious diseases (established but incomplete) {2.4.3, 2.5} and global temperatures and other climatic changes (well established) {2.5.2.2}. Rising global food demand, driven by affluence in particular, has led to an increase in agricultural production." ;
    dcterms:identifier "2.4.2, 2.5, 2.4.3, 2.5.2.2" .

